## Summary

Implemented **US-208 — inserting a new section in the middle of a lesson** following the existing US-146 regenerate_section pattern, but with the route owning persistence (no separate Apply step).

**Files added:**
- `scripts/ralph/skills/insert_section/insert_section.md` — new generation skill (sibling of `regenerate_section`). Reads `{ lessonContext, anchorSectionId, instruction }` from stdin, emits exactly one `{ newSection }` (default `theory`).
- `src/lib/schemas/insertSection.ts` — `InsertSectionRequestSchema` + `InsertSectionResponseSchema` (validates against `SectionSchema`).
- `src/lib/server/insertSection.ts` — spawn helper mirroring `regenerateSection.ts` (model pin, working-memory pointers, test-injectable spawn) + pure `makeUniqueSectionId`.
- `.../sections/[sectionId]/insert/route.ts` — POST: validate → busy gate → read lesson → find anchor → run agent → assign collision-free id → splice **directly after** the anchor → re-validate `LessonSchema` → snapshot `.lesson-prev.json` → `atomicWriteJson`.
- `.../sections/[sectionId]/insert/undo/route.ts` — restores the snapshot byte-for-byte.
- `src/lib/server/insertSection.test.ts` — 22 tests.

**Acceptance criteria coverage:**
- ✅ New skill generates exactly one section, Zod-validated
- ✅ Route spawns `claude -p` (regenerateSection pattern), inserts after `[sectionId]`, atomic write
- ✅ Snapshot + working undo path
- ✅ Unique id, existing sections untouched in content + order
- ✅ Timeout/invalid output → structured HTTP error with **zero** file modification (write happens only after agent success + schema validation)
- ✅ Tests: middle/last insertion, id uniqueness, invalid-output rejection, undo
- ✅ Typecheck clean; 22/22 new tests pass

The one failing test in the broader sweep (`generation.test.ts > writes a .generating.json marker…`) is a pre-existing flaky timing test — it passes in isolation and I never touched `generation.ts`. `prd.json` `US-208.passes` is confirmed `true` in HEAD (commit `825ba42`).
